package "products / PostgreSQL" {
 entity "reservation_signals" as reservation_signals {
  order_guid : UUID <<PK>>
  product_guid : UUID
  state : VARCHAR(20)
  updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
 }
}
package "orders / PostgreSQL" {
 entity "payment_signals" as payment_signals {
  order_guid : UUID <<PK>>
  payment_guid : UUID
  topic : VARCHAR(40)
  received_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
 }
 entity "order_confirmations" as confirmations {
  order_guid : UUID <<PK, FK orders.guid>>
  document : BYTEA
  created_at : TIMESTAMPTZ
 }
}
orders_orders "1" -- "0..1" confirmations : order_guid
orders_orders_details ..> users_users : user_guid = guid (logical reference)
orders_orders_details ..> products_products : product_guid = guid (logical reference)
payments_payments_details ..> orders_orders : order_guid = guid (logical reference)
payments_payments_details ..> products_products : product_guid = guid (logical reference)
orders_orders_details ..> payments_payments : payment_guid = guid (logical reference)
products_products_details ..> orders_orders : reserved_order_guid = guid (logical reference)
products_products ..> mongo_product : guid / asynchronous projection
note bottom of mongo_product
  Tombstones (deleted=true) hide removed cars and reject stale events.
  Nested numeric types follow the JSON snapshot; price is Decimal128.
  Product View is the sole MongoDB owner.
  Synchronizer accesses the projection only through the internal API.
end note
legend bottom
  PK = primary key, FK = local foreign key, UQ = unique constraint
  Dashed dependencies across databases are logical UUID references, never SQL FKs.
  SQL timestamps follow the current JPA mappings; no field is added by this diagram.
  Outbox/inbox and active workers exist in every SQL-owning service.
endlegend
package "Keycloak / PostgreSQL (identity infrastructure)" {
  entity "Keycloak managed schema" as keycloak_store <<identity>>
}
note bottom of keycloak_store
  Keycloak owns and migrates its identity schema.
  Business services do not read these tables.
  Protected customerGuid attributes reference Users UUIDs logically.
  Self-registration uses stable issuer/subject linkage, not email matching.
  Internal Keycloak tables are outside the domain model shown here.
end note
@enduml
